# Copy to client/.env.local for local overrides. NEVER put a real key here —
# this file is tracked by git.

# --- Deployed (Vercel) -------------------------------------------------------
# Set GEMINI_API_KEY in the Vercel dashboard (Project → Settings → Environment
# Variables), NOT in this repo. It is read by the serverless function in
# client/api/generate.ts and is never exposed to the browser.
# GEMINI_API_KEY=your_gemini_api_key_here
# Optional: override the image model (defaults to gemini-3.1-flash-lite-image)
# GEMINI_IMAGE_MODEL=gemini-3.1-flash-lite-image

# Uploads the cropped tile photo and the 3 generated concepts to Google Drive
# instead of returning them as base64. Read by client/api/_lib/googleDrive.ts.
# The two folder ids point at two DIFFERENT Drive folders — one for cropped
# tile photos, one for generated concepts. All four are required together —
# if any is missing, generation still works, it just falls back to returning
# the images inline instead of as Drive links (see uploadOrFallback in
# client/api/_lib/generateVisualization.ts).
#
# GOOGLE_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_EMAIL — the "client_email" field from the service
# account's JSON key (Google Cloud Console → IAM & Admin → Service Accounts →
# your account → Keys → Add key → JSON).
# GOOGLE_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_EMAIL=your-service-account@your-project.iam.gserviceaccount.com
#
# GOOGLE_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_PRIVATE_KEY — the "private_key" field from that same
# JSON key, including the -----BEGIN/END PRIVATE KEY----- lines. Paste it as
# one line with literal \n where the line breaks are — that is how the JSON
# file itself stores it, and how Vercel's dashboard expects a multi-line
# secret in a single-line env var. The code un-escapes those \n back into
# real newlines before use.
# GOOGLE_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_PRIVATE_KEY="-----BEGIN PRIVATE KEY-----\nMIIEvQ...\n-----END PRIVATE KEY-----\n"
#
# GOOGLE_DRIVE_CROP_FOLDER_ID — where cropped tile source photos are uploaded.
# Share this folder with the service account's email (Editor access), then
# copy its ID out of the folder's URL — the part after /folders/:
# https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/THIS_PART_HERE
# GOOGLE_DRIVE_CROP_FOLDER_ID=your_crop_folder_id_here
#
# GOOGLE_DRIVE_GENERATED_FOLDER_ID — where the 3 generated concept images are
# uploaded. A separate folder from the one above; share it with the service
# account the same way and copy its ID the same way.
# GOOGLE_DRIVE_GENERATED_FOLDER_ID=your_generated_folder_id_here

# --- Local development -------------------------------------------------------
# The app calls same-origin /api/generate. `npm run dev` proxies /api to the
# local Express server in server/ (default http://localhost:3001).
# Point the dev proxy somewhere else:
# VITE_DEV_API_PROXY=http://localhost:3001
# Call a fully different API host instead of same-origin (rarely needed):
# VITE_API_BASE_URL=https://your-api-host.example.com
